    "# Module 8 Solutions: Information Theory\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook contains complete solutions and working Python code for the Module 8 exercises."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1. Information Content of Card Draws\n",
    "There are 4 Aces in a deck of 52 cards. So the probability $P(\\text{Ace}) = 4/52 = 1/13$.\n",
    "Self-information:\n",
    "$$I(\\text{Ace}) = -\\log_2(1/13) = \\log_2(13) \\approx 3.7004 \\text{ bits}$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "p_ace = 4 / 52\n",
    "i_ace = -np.log2(p_ace)\n",
    "print(f\"Self-information of drawing an Ace: {i_ace:.4f} bits\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2. Shannon Entropy of a Uniform Distribution\n",
    "For a fair 8-sided die, there are $K=8$ outcomes each with probability $1/8$.\n",
    "$$H(X) = -\\sum_{i=1}^8 \\frac{1}{8} \\log_2\\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right) = \\log_2(8) = 3 \\text{ bits}$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "p = np.ones(8) / 8\n",
    "entropy = -np.sum(p * np.log2(p))\n",
    "print(f\"Entropy of a fair 8-sided die: {entropy:.4f} bits\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3. Cross-Entropy Loss Calculation\n",
    "For $y = [0, 1, 0]$ and $\\hat{y} = [0.1, 0.7, 0.2]$:\n",
    "$$\\text{Cross-Entropy} = -\\sum_{i} y_i \\ln \\hat{y}_i = - (0 \\cdot \\ln(0.1) + 1 \\cdot \\ln(0.7) + 0 \\cdot \\ln(0.2)) = -\\ln(0.7) \\approx 0.3567$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "y = np.array([0, 1, 0])\n",
    "y_hat = np.array([0.1, 0.7, 0.2])\n",
    "loss = -np.sum(y * np.log(y_hat))\n",
    "print(f\"Categorical Cross-Entropy Loss: {loss:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4. Bounds of Entropy\n",
    "- **Lower bound ($0$)**: $H(X) \\ge 0$ since $P(x) \\ge 0$ and $\\log_2 P(x) \\le 0$ for all $P(x) \\in [0, 1]$. The minimum value is reached when some $P(x_i) = 1$, representing a completely deterministic outcome.\n",
    "- **Upper bound ($\\log_2(K)$)**: By Jensen's Inequality, since $\\log$ is concave:\n",
    "  $$H(X) = \\sum P(x) \\log_2 \\frac{1}{P(x)} \\le \\log_2 \\left( \\sum P(x) \\frac{1}{P(x)} \\right) = \\log_2(K)$$\n",
    "  Equality holds if and only if $P(x) = 1/K$ for all $x$ (uniform distribution)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Theoretical proof."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 5. KL Divergence Non-Negativity Proof\n",
    "Using Jensen's Inequality for the strictly convex function $-\\ln(t)$:\n",
    "$$D_{KL}(P \\parallel Q) = - \\sum_x P(x) \\ln \\frac{Q(x)}{P(x)} \\ge - \\ln \\left( \\sum_x P(x) \\frac{Q(x)}{P(x)} \\right) = - \\ln \\left( \\sum_x Q(x) \\right) = -\\ln(1) = 0$$\n",
    "Thus, $D_{KL}(P \\parallel Q) \\ge 0$. Since $-\\ln(t)$ is strictly convex, equality holds if and only if $Q(x)/P(x) = 1$ everywhere, i.e., $P = Q$."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Theoretical proof."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 6. Mutual Information and Independence\n",
    "If $X$ and $Y$ are independent, $P(x, y) = P(x)P(y)$.\n",
    "$$I(X; Y) = \\sum_{x, y} P(x, y) \\log \\frac{P(x, y)}{P(x)P(y)} = \\sum_{x, y} P(x)P(y) \\log(1) = 0$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Theoretical proof."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 7. Conditional Entropy Identity\n",
    "$$H(Y|X) = -\\sum_{x, y} P(x, y) \\log P(y|x)$$\n",
    "Using $P(y|x) = \\frac{P(x, y)}{P(x)}$:\n",
    "$$H(Y|X) = -\\sum_{x, y} P(x, y) \\log \\frac{P(x, y)}{P(x)} = -\\sum_{x, y} P(x, y) \\log P(x, y) + \\sum_{x, y} P(x, y) \\log P(x)$$\n",
    "$$= H(X, Y) + \\sum_x P(x) \\log P(x) = H(X, Y) - H(X)$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Theoretical proof."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 8. Information Bottleneck Formulation\n",
    "The Information Bottleneck objective is:\n",
    "$$\\min_{p(z|x)} I(X; Z) - \\beta I(Y; Z)$$\n",
    "where $Z$ is a compressed representation of $X$. \n",
    "- Minimizing $I(X; Z)$ forces the model to discard irrelevant information from $X$.\n",
    "- Maximizing $I(Y; Z)$ forces the model to retain information in $Z$ that is useful for predicting $Y$."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Theoretical description."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 9. KL Divergence between two 1D Gaussians\n",
    "For $P \\sim \\mathcal{N}(\\mu_1, \\sigma_1^2)$ and $Q \\sim \\mathcal{N}(\\mu_2, \\sigma_2^2)$:\n",
    "$$D_{KL}(P \\parallel Q) = \\log \\frac{\\sigma_2}{\\sigma_1} + \\frac{\\sigma_1^2 + (\\mu_1 - \\mu_2)^2}{2\\sigma_2^2} - \\frac{1}{2}$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def kl_gaussians(mu1, sigma1, mu2, sigma2):\n",
    "    return np.log(sigma2 / sigma1) + (sigma1**2 + (mu1 - mu2)**2) / (2 * sigma2**2) - 0.5\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"KL(N(0, 1) || N(1, 2)):\", kl_gaussians(0.0, 1.0, 1.0, 2.0))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 10. Verify VAE KL Divergence Loss in Python\n",
    "For $q(z|x) = \\mathcal{N}(\\mu, \\text{diag}(\\sigma^2))$ and $p(z) = \\mathcal{N}(0, I)$:\n",
    "$$D_{KL}(q(z|x) \\parallel p(z)) = -\\frac{1}{2} \\sum_{j=1}^J \\left( 1 + \\log(\\sigma_j^2) - \\mu_j^2 - \\sigma_j^2 \\right)$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def vae_kl_loss(mu, log_var):\n",
    "    return -0.5 * np.sum(1 + log_var - mu**2 - np.exp(log_var))\n",
    "\n",
    "mu = np.array([0.1, -0.2])\n",
    "log_var = np.array([0.0, -0.1])\n",
    "print(\"VAE KL Loss:\", vae_kl_loss(mu, log_var))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 11. Joint and Conditional Entropy of a Binary Symmetric Channel\n",
    "For a BSC with crossover probability $p$, input $X$ (assumed uniform $P(X=0)=P(X=1)=0.5$) and output $Y$:\n",
    "- $H(Y|X) = - p \\log_2(p) - (1-p) \\log_2(1-p) = H_b(p)$ (the binary entropy function).\n",
    "- Since $X$ is uniform and the channel is symmetric, $Y$ is also uniform, so $H(Y) = 1$ bit.\n",
    "- Capacity $C = \\max_{P(x)} I(X; Y) = \\max_{P(x)} (H(Y) - H(Y|X)) = 1 - H_b(p)$."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "binary_entropy = lambda p: -p * np.log2(p) - (1 - p) * np.log2(1 - p) if 0 < p < 1 else 0\n",
    "print(\"Capacity for p = 0.1:\", 1 - binary_entropy(0.1))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 12. Text Processing: Entropy of a Corpus"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from collections import Counter\n",
    "\n",
    "corpus = \"the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog\"\n",
    "counts = Counter(corpus)\n",
    "total = len(corpus)\n",
    "probabilities = [count / total for count in counts.values()]\n",
    "\n",
    "entropy = -sum(p * np.log2(p) for p in probabilities)\n",
    "print(f\"Character-level entropy of corpus: {entropy:.4f} bits\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 13. Mutual Information for Feature Selection"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.datasets import make_classification\n",
    "from sklearn.feature_selection import mutual_info_classif\n",
    "\n",
    "X, y = make_classification(n_samples=200, n_features=5, n_informative=2, random_state=42)\n",
    "mi_scores = mutual_info_classif(X, y)\n",
    "for i, score in enumerate(mi_scores):\n",
    "    print(f\"Feature {i} MI Score: {score:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 14. Jensen-Shannon Divergence\n",
    "$$JSD(P \\parallel Q) = \\frac{1}{2} D_{KL}(P \\parallel M) + \\frac{1}{2} D_{KL}(Q \\parallel M)$$\n",
    "where $M = \\frac{1}{2}(P + Q)$."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def jsd(p, q):\n",
    "    p = np.array(p)\n",
    "    q = np.array(q)\n",
    "    m = 0.5 * (p + q)\n",
    "    def kl(x, y):\n",
    "        return np.sum(x * np.log(x / y))\n",
    "    return 0.5 * kl(p, m) + 0.5 * kl(q, m)\n",
    "\n",
    "p = [0.1, 0.9]\n",
    "q = [0.8, 0.2]\n",
    "print(\"JSD(P || Q):\", jsd(p, q))\n",
    "print(\"JSD(Q || P):\", jsd(q, p))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 15. Maximize Entropy of a Discrete Distribution with constraints\n",
    "Maximize $H(p) = -\\sum p_i \\ln p_i$ subject to $\\sum p_i = 1$.\n",
    "Lagrangian:\n",
    "$$\\mathcal{L}(p, \\lambda) = -\\sum_{i=1}^K p_i \\ln p_i - \\lambda \\left(\\sum_{i=1}^K p_i - 1\\right)$$\n",
    "Taking derivative w.r.t. $p_i$ and setting to zero:\n",
    "$$\\frac{\\partial \\mathcal{L}}{\\partial p_i} = -\\ln p_i - 1 - \\lambda = 0 \\implies p_i = e^{-(1+\\lambda)}$$\n",
    "Since $p_i$ is independent of $i$, all $p_i$ must be equal. Since they sum to 1, we must have $p_i = 1/K$ for all $i$ (uniform distribution)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
